3. VOY Recruiting Announcement （ENG）.pdf,2023년 03월 16일 17시 10분 40초,취업지원과,160549,"<Asia Society Korea Young Fellowship: 2023 Voice of Youth> 
 
Since 2018, Asia Society Korea has been supporting talented young minds who wish to 
refine and achieve their academic pursuits beyond the boundary of the school. Listening 
to the voices of the younger generation, “Voice of Youth” is a program that supports 
student research on diverse issues that impact both South Korea and the world. 
Asia Society Korea is recruiting the sixth class for the Voice of Youth (VOY) 
program. This exciting opportunity to expand your research ability will support you by 
providing research funding, research assistance, networking opportunities, and 
publication. In addition, you will receive publication and earn a certificate of completion 
upon report submission.  
1. Research Topics (Topics can be chosen freely within the four main subject areas) 
• 
Arts & Culture: Research in various areas such as art, music, literature, and 
culture. 
• 
Education: Research on the education system of developed countries along with 
policy suggestions. 
• 
Policy & Society: Research on East Asian political issues and domestic social 
issues. 
• 
Business & Economy: Research on prospects for future industries and economic 
development. 
2. Qualifications 
• 
Undergraduate or graduate student at a South Korean university. 
• 
Majoring in a relevant field. 
• 
Can participate in various events during the program. 
• 
An interest in current affairs and social issues. 
• 
Able to research and write in English.  
3. Benefits 
• 
Networking opportunities and research assistance will be provided. 
• 
Invitations to attend monthly luncheons and seminars hosted by Asia Society 
Korea. 
• 
Final research papers will be published in a special volume and a VOY program 
certificate will be awarded. 
• 
Asia Society Korea's Student Membership will be given to the researcher with the 
most outstanding performance. 
• 
Maximum of 1,000,000 KRW will be funded towards research. 
 
 
 
 
4. 2023 Schedule 
• 
April 20, 2023, at 18:00: Deadline for applications. 
• 
April 26-28, 2023: 30-minute interviews 
• 
May 4, 2023: Selection process completed. 
• 
May 2023: Orientation. 
• 
May 2023: Deadline for revised research proposals and budget plan. 
• 
